        "evidence": "Three isotypes of S_3 - a complete, forced enumeration. MATH FINDINGS recorded here (see notes).",
        "notes": "STANDING-TRAP FINDINGS, report only, do not fix inline. (1) DIMENSION CLUSTER: three mutually inconsistent statements about the same V in consecutive sentences. The display gives V = V_(3) + V_(1,1,1) + V_(2,1) = Sym^3 + Alt^3 + Std^{+2}, which has dimension 1+1+2*2 = 6 - that is the REGULAR representation R[S_3] (and the sibling proposition correctly writes R[S_3] = R + R + R^{2x2}), not V. The next sentence says the dimensions are 1, 1, 2, 'summing to 4' - arithmetically right for irrep dimensions but not the dimension of anything, and inconsistent with the Std^{+2} just displayed. The sentence after that corrects to V = V_(3) + V_(2,1), rank 3, which is the CORRECT statement and the one the rest of the proof uses (it is why the Alt piece has to be found inside Lambda^3 V). So the first display and the dimension sentence are stale and contradict the proof's own working. (2) The same V is defined as a tensor product (dim 1 over C, as a product of three tangent lines) and then identified with the free module R<dc_1/dz, dc_2/dz, dc_3/dz> (rank 3); the isomorphism sign should be a direct sum. Later the projector is applied 'to ... in V^{tensor 3}', a third meaning of V. (3) CORRECT AND CHECKED: the sign projector (1/6)(id - (12) - (13) - (23) + (123) + (132)) has the right signs; V_3^2 = Delta and (prod dc_k/dz)^2 = V_3^2/Delta^2 = 1/Delta is consistent. (4) NOTATION: 'the scalar weight w_lambda from the Markov trace' - AGENTS.md 7aa separates y_lambda, w_lambda and tilde-w_lambda as distinct families at q != 1, and the corpus's Markov-trace coefficients are y_lambda (prop:y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge). Confirm which family is meant."
